// THE SHIP'S FOOD STORES (increment 3 of docs/design/ship-homes-and-logistics.md; the relay's
// src/relay/handlers/ship_stores.rs). Read by the relay at startup, disk first, the copy built
// into the exe only when this file is missing.
//
// The operator decided on 2026-10-04 (that design's open question 12): NPCs eat from the same
// food stores as players, and NPC homesteads mostly provide for themselves. So each store here
// is ONE stock of meals that everyone eats from: a crew member who eats takes one at the end of
// its meal in the mess hall (data/npc/chores.ron, `meal: true`), and a player takes one with
// the `take_meal` action on the store, one a meal interval per person like the crew (the game's
// own hunger does not read it yet; serving meals into the food system is the design's
// increment 6).
//
// Every time here is on the shared world's GAME clock, which runs at the server setting
// `world_time_scale` (72x by default: a game day is 20 real minutes). Meals come on it and the
// farms fill the stores on it, so the balance below holds at any speed an admin sets. Only the
// crew's walking and their chores' lengths (data/npc/chores.ron, a meal's 40 s included) are
// real seconds, so a figure never sprints; at 72x that makes a crew member's meal (8 game
// hours apart = 400 real seconds) a walk to the mess hall and 40 s at the table about every
// 7 real minutes.
//
// UNLIMITED OR STOCKED (the operator, 2026-10-04: "For the sake of simplicity during early
// development we'll say the fleet has unlimited of everything and just track what they player
// uses and contributes."). The server setting `fleet_supply_mode` (Server Settings > ADMIN >
// Fleet supply) says which: "unlimited", the default, where a meal is always there and the
// stock below is never drawn on, so nobody misses a meal; or "stocked", the realistic mode, where
// everything below holds exactly as written. In both, a meal a player takes is a "used" line of
// their fleet ledger (data/ship/fleet_ledger.ron prices it), and what they give the fleet is
// the other side of it.
//
// Every number below is a game default chosen for this increment, NOT a sourced figure.
//
//   stores        one row per store: id, label, the room it stands in (`place`, a room id of the
//                 relay's world), where in that room (`spot`, room-local x and z metres, like a
//                 chore's), the meals a new world starts with, and the most it holds.
//   meal_interval_hours
//                 game hours between one person's meals: 8 is three a day.
//   empty_store_retry_minutes
//                 game minutes until a crew member who found the store empty comes back to try
//                 again (a homestead NPC, with food of its own, waits for its next meal time).
//   ship_farms_meals_per_day
//                 what fills the stores today: a stand-in for the ship's farms (the agricultural
//                 bay, the Commons garden) until goods are really carried aboard (the design's
//                 increment 9, shipments). What players give the fleet is recorded in their
//                 ledger and does not fill this stock yet. Meals per GAME day: 18
//                 feeds the five crew who eat (15 a day at three meals each) with a little over
//                 for players.
//   npc_homestead_self_provided
//                 the operator's "NPC homesteads should mostly provide for themselves": the share
//                 of an NPC homestead household's meals its own homestead grows (crew.ron
//                 `household: "homestead"`); the rest come from these stores. 0.8 is "mostly".
//                 No shipped NPC lives on a homestead yet, so this waits for the first ones.
//   npc_homestead_fleet_meals_per_day
//                 Meals a day that EACH NPC homestead household puts into these stores.
//                 ANSWERED by the operator on 2026-10-04: "We'll keep it to 0 for now. Once we
//                 get the player stuff sorted we'll worry about NPCs for the market." So 0.0;
//                 like the share above it, it changes nothing until an NPC lives on a homestead.
(
    stores: [
        (
            id: "mess-hall-stores",
            label: "The mess hall's stores",
            place: "mess-hall",
            spot: (2.0, 2.0),
            meals: 90.0,
            capacity: 300.0,
        ),
    ],
    meal_interval_hours: 8.0,
    empty_store_retry_minutes: 30.0,
    ship_farms_meals_per_day: 18.0,
    npc_homestead_self_provided: 0.8,
    npc_homestead_fleet_meals_per_day: 0.0,
)
